d_exposure.rb, and does not present it as a mere stand-in. Does not give Kochnev's 62-76% share of the directory.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Credits Lena Brandt, the only active contributor, with about 11% of the delegator code and says Kochnev has 66.7%. The truth is that nobody active owns any line. An active person is named as an owner.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Credits Marco with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb, when it was copied from Kochnev's file. Does not give a repo-wide share for Marco. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Credits Lena Brandt with 18 lines and recommends her as a reviewer. Gives no departed share of 79-90%. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Says dblock has the most commits and Kochnev has the most lines, so they are different people. Gives no percentages. Does not put Kochnev's share at 21-29% or dblock's at 3-8%, and dblock is not shown at 5.6% of lines. Lacks the quantitative content.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Names Marco Silva as primary reviewer for exposure with 147 lines, and gives no 69% Kochnev share. Does not say that active owners hold at most 8%. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Names Marco Silva as primary reviewer for the delegator code. Does not say nobody active owns it. Credits Marco with the rename but not with the code lines in the delegator, though the 147 lines are combined across both areas. Gives no Kochnev share of 68-82%. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Credits Marco with 147 surviving lines, and does not trace the copied grouped_exposure.rb back to Kochnev. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Credits Lena with 30 lines and recommends her as a second reviewer. Gives no departed share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Says dblock has the most commits (38, aliases unmerged), and does not give percentages or Kochnev's repo-wide share. For exposure it says the top committer is the top owner. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Says Kochnev owns about half of exposure (431 of 800+), which is below the 62-76% range. Recommends Marco Silva as primary reviewer without calling it a stand-in. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Gives Kochnev 59% of the delegator code, below the 68-82% range. Names Lena and Marco as reviewers with 10 of 102 lines. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Credits Marco with 143 lines in exposure and does not trace grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Gives Lena 20 lines and as backup reviewer, with no departed share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Gives dblock 52 commits (18.2%) and 10.4% of lines, and Kochnev 18.7% of lines. Both are outside the ranges, and the names are only partly merged. The direction is right but the numbers are not.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Gives Kochnev 54% of exposure, below 62-76%. Recommends Marco for grouped_exposure.rb and Anna as second. Reports 19.9% held by active people, versus the 2.6% truth. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Gives Kochnev 71% of the delegator code, which is in range. But it credits active Marco with 4 lines (4.1%), when nobody active owns any line in the truth scope. It does not credit the rename as code. It says 95.9% belongs to inactive people, not 100%. The criterion's FAIL clause for an active person named as owner is borderline, but 4% is a small and honest figure. Still fails on the no-active-owner requirement.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Says merged Marco is about 2.6% of the repo, above the 2% limit. Credits 117 lines of grouped_exposure.rb to Marco's laptop address and does not trace it to Kochnev. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Gives 89.3% of lines to people with no commit in the last 365 days, which is in range. Does not mention Lena Brandt having 0 lines. Does not mention Scholz's 4% or Subbota's 3.3% in the required way, and says peter scholz has 14 lines in exposure. Misses several parts. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Says dblock has the most commits but 'about 34' lines, and Kochnev has about 756 lines in lib/. Gives no percentages and not 5.6%. Does identify Kochnev as top owner who left in 2015. The numbers are not in range, and dblock's lines are far too low.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Names Lena, Anna and Marco as reviewers for exposure. Gives no 69% Kochnev share and no active-owner share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Names Marco as best reviewer for the delegator code. Gives no Kochnev share and does not say nobody active owns it. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Credits Marco with 143 lines in lib/, about 2.8%, above 2%. Does not trace grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Treats Lena as one of two people who can review. Gives no departed share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Says Doubrovkine has about 117 commits across name variants, which is close to the truth. Kochnev has the most code (758 in lib/) and left in 2015. But no percentages are given. Does not give dblock's low line share, only 'little'. The ranges are not met, though the merge is correct.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Recommends Marco Silva as the only active person with substantial code in exposure, and gives no Kochnev 69% share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Names Marco as reviewer for the delegator code. Does not give Kochnev's share and does not say nobody active owns it. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Credits Marco with 147 lines and says counts 'could still be inflated by the rename'. Does not trace grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Credits Lena with 30 surviving lines. Gives no departed share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":17309,"type":"result","duration_ms":17334,"u